WEBVTT

1

00:00:39.667 --> 00:00:43.875

I should've known... this would happen.



2

00:00:44.958 --> 00:00:50.083

But... I had no other choice but to rely on you.



3

00:00:50.083 --> 00:00:51.500

Armin...



4

00:00:52.625 --> 00:00:56.292

Why... don't you run away?



5

00:01:03.208 --> 00:01:04.833

A Titan?



6

00:01:10.375 --> 00:01:11.708

Shit!



7

00:01:14.042 --> 00:01:16.292

You just try coming closer!



8

00:01:16.292 --> 00:01:19.375

Make one move to take him and he's dead!



9

00:01:21.042 --> 00:01:23.125

What's that?



10

00:01:23.125 --> 00:01:27.917

He's got... Titan marks around his eyes.



11

00:01:27.917 --> 00:01:30.750

Is he the Beast Titan?!



12

00:01:30.750 --> 00:01:33.125

Are you...



13

00:01:33.125 --> 00:01:35.667

...Eren Jaeger?



14

00:01:35.667 --> 00:01:38.500

If nothing else, I'm taking him with me!



15

00:01:38.500 --> 00:01:41.500

You look nothing like your father.



16

00:01:46.125 --> 00:01:47.542

What?



17

00:01:48.792 --> 00:01:54.042

Believe me, I know what you're going through.



18

00:01:54.042 --> 00:01:57.750

We're both victims of your father.



19

00:01:57.750 --> 00:02:01.500

You've... been brainwashed by him.



20

00:02:04.458 --> 00:02:06.500

My... dad?



21

00:02:09.083 --> 00:02:12.042

Argh... You're kidding me!



22

00:02:12.042 --> 00:02:14.292

He chased me all the way here?



23

00:02:21.542 --> 00:02:26.417

Let's call it a draw, Levi.

We're in no shape to fight.



24

00:02:26.417 --> 00:02:28.083

Bertholdt...



25

00:02:28.083 --> 00:02:31.667

I'm sorry, but I think it's the end for you.



26

00:02:33.375 --> 00:02:37.333

Eren! Someday, I'm coming back to rescue you!



27

00:02:42.333 --> 00:02:43.792

He ran?



28

00:02:47.083 --> 00:02:48.792

Captain!



29

00:02:48.792 --> 00:02:50.625

That was the last of my gas.



30

00:02:50.625 --> 00:02:53.417

I'll chase him! Hand over your gas and blades!



31

00:02:53.417 --> 00:02:54.333

Right!



32

00:02:54.333 --> 00:02:55.583

Hurry!



33

00:03:11.792 --> 00:03:17.125

Reiner... What's this metal case

you had in your left chest pocket?



34

00:03:17.125 --> 00:03:19.875

Before we chopped off all your limbs,



35

00:03:19.875 --> 00:03:23.625

you tried to grab it with

the strength you had left.



36

00:03:23.625 --> 00:03:27.292

Suicide pills? Or perhaps a bomb?



37

00:03:27.292 --> 00:03:28.583

Ouch!



38

00:03:28.583 --> 00:03:29.833

Sorry.



39

00:03:31.625 --> 00:03:33.250

A letter...



40

00:03:33.250 --> 00:03:35.167

A letter?



41

00:03:35.167 --> 00:03:37.417

What kind of letter?



42

00:03:37.417 --> 00:03:41.333

A letter... from Ymir.



43

00:03:41.333 --> 00:03:47.167

You have to... give it... to Christa...



44

00:03:48.875 --> 00:03:51.667

Only after we've inspected it.



45

00:03:54.667 --> 00:03:59.042

Now then. I've got a mountain

of questions for you, but...



46

00:04:00.875 --> 00:04:05.125

Your lips seem as tight as your armor is hard.



47

00:04:05.125 --> 00:04:10.792

Are you going to cooperate and tell us

everything that we want to know?



48

00:04:10.792 --> 00:04:12.333

No.



49

00:04:12.333 --> 00:04:16.250

Thanks. It helps that you're prepared for this.



50

00:04:19.167 --> 00:04:20.875

Hold on!



51

00:04:20.875 --> 00:04:24.833

Are you sure? We might be able

to steal his power.



52

00:04:29.000 --> 00:04:31.083

Today, I would like to explain...



53

00:04:31.083 --> 00:04:36.000

...how we're going to get

maximum value from this injection.



54

00:04:36.000 --> 00:04:40.417

Using this medicine, the Colossal

Titan's, the Armored Titan's,



55

00:04:40.417 --> 00:04:44.333

or the Beast Titan's powers can be stolen.



56

00:04:44.333 --> 00:04:46.167

As for how...



57

00:04:46.167 --> 00:04:49.083

The one injected with this will become a Titan



58

00:04:49.083 --> 00:04:53.083

and eat someone who can change

into a Titan like Eren can.



59

00:04:53.083 --> 00:04:57.708

By doing so, although they would

initially be a Titan lacking intelligence,



60

00:04:57.708 --> 00:05:02.333

they would revert into a human

able to wield that Titan's powers.



61

00:05:03.417 --> 00:05:08.917

If this is achieved, not only do we gain

information regarding Titan powers,



62

00:05:08.917 --> 00:05:13.875

we're also able to revive a person

on the brink of death.



63

00:05:13.875 --> 00:05:18.417

If you capture an enemy with

Titan powers, sever all their limbs.



64

00:05:18.417 --> 00:05:23.125

And when it is safe to do so,

summon Captain Levi.



65

00:05:25.708 --> 00:05:28.250

We have only this one injection.



66

00:05:28.250 --> 00:05:32.083

I'm entrusting Captain Levi

with the call to use it.



67

00:05:34.042 --> 00:05:38.042

I don't think all the conditions

for that have been met.



68

00:05:38.042 --> 00:05:41.167

We don't know the situation

with Levi and the other side.



69

00:05:41.167 --> 00:05:45.042

Neither do we have the time

to go confirm it ourselves.



70

00:05:45.042 --> 00:05:51.208

Reason being, there's no way for us

to gauge the full depth of their powers!



71

00:05:51.208 --> 00:05:54.833

Even if I cut his head off,

we can't be too sure!



72

00:05:59.042 --> 00:06:01.750

This isn't like you, Hange.



73

00:06:03.417 --> 00:06:06.500

If we back down because

of not knowing something,



74

00:06:06.500 --> 00:06:10.667

down the line, can we ever

hope to beat the Titans?



75

00:06:13.375 --> 00:06:14.958

Jean...



76

00:06:14.958 --> 00:06:20.000

When are we ever going to know

all there is about the enemy?



77

00:06:23.042 --> 00:06:24.208

Mikasa.



78

00:06:24.208 --> 00:06:25.167

Yeah?



79

00:06:25.167 --> 00:06:27.333

How much gas do you have?



80

00:06:27.333 --> 00:06:29.750

It's almost entirely gone.



81

00:06:29.750 --> 00:06:34.375

But it should be enough to reach

Eren and Armin at least.



82

00:06:34.375 --> 00:06:36.583

That's more than me.



83

00:06:38.875 --> 00:06:43.333

Mikasa... I need you to go

check out their situation.



84

00:06:43.333 --> 00:06:48.125

Fill up your gas and bring back

the injection from Levi.



85

00:06:48.125 --> 00:06:53.125

If for any reason you're unable

to do so, fire a smoke signal.



86

00:06:53.125 --> 00:06:55.833

That will be my signal to end Reiner.



87

00:06:57.083 --> 00:06:58.542

Affirmative.



88

00:07:03.667 --> 00:07:04.875

Hange, I--



89

00:07:04.875 --> 00:07:07.000

The decision was mine.



90

00:07:07.000 --> 00:07:09.333

You were just a factor.



91

00:07:10.458 --> 00:07:13.333

Why... did I?



92

00:07:13.333 --> 00:07:16.208

After all this time, am I actually...?



93

00:07:16.208 --> 00:07:18.583

Yeah! Keep it up!



94

00:07:20.458 --> 00:07:22.958

Armin's breathing again!



95

00:07:24.500 --> 00:07:27.917

Come on! Just keep on breathing!



96

00:07:31.417 --> 00:07:32.833

Armin?



97

00:07:32.833 --> 00:07:35.625

Captain! Get the syringe!



98

00:07:43.125 --> 00:07:47.083

Make Armin into a Titan and

we'll have him eat Bertholdt!



99

00:07:47.083 --> 00:07:49.167

Hurry up and inject him!



100

00:07:51.750 --> 00:07:53.125

Yeah...



101

00:08:02.292 --> 00:08:03.708

Hange!



102

00:08:14.208 --> 00:08:15.458

Not good!



103

00:08:23.792 --> 00:08:26.583

Reiner was taken! Hange!



104

00:08:27.792 --> 00:08:28.917

Shit!



105

00:08:28.917 --> 00:08:31.417

Conny! Don't chase!



106

00:08:34.792 --> 00:08:39.250

We hardly have any gas left.

You'll just end up getting killed.



107

00:08:39.250 --> 00:08:41.167

Shit!



108

00:08:42.375 --> 00:08:44.083

It's my fault...



109

00:08:44.083 --> 00:08:48.708

I've... done something terrible...



110

00:08:48.708 --> 00:08:51.958

I said the decision was mine.



111

00:08:51.958 --> 00:08:54.208

Let's regroup with the others.



112

00:09:02.833 --> 00:09:05.875

Captain... Levi...



113

00:09:05.875 --> 00:09:08.542

I finally found you.



114

00:09:08.542 --> 00:09:11.167

Commander Erwin is badly wounded!



115

00:09:11.167 --> 00:09:14.958

His stomach is gouged...

and his organs are demolished!



116

00:09:14.958 --> 00:09:17.750

The blood just won't stop!



117

00:09:17.750 --> 00:09:21.250

I thought that injection

might be able to help, but...



118

00:09:21.250 --> 00:09:22.875

What do you think?



119

00:09:28.500 --> 00:09:29.833

Huh?



120

00:09:37.125 --> 00:09:38.583

Captain?



121

00:09:44.125 --> 00:09:46.917

He's... still breathing.



122

00:09:48.417 --> 00:09:52.125

He's... alive.



123

00:10:03.417 --> 00:10:06.625

I'm using the injection... on Erwin.



124

00:10:10.708 --> 00:10:12.500

You said...



125

00:10:12.500 --> 00:10:14.833

...you'd use it on Armin!



126

00:10:15.958 --> 00:10:20.333

I'm... reviving the one who can save humanity.



127

00:10:34.667 --> 00:10:38.917

Reiner... You were incredibly lucky.



128

00:10:41.000 --> 00:10:46.000

"Not only can Titan powers and much-needed information

be stolen by using the injection, but it also allows

the revival of someone who is critically wounded.

The ideal candidate would be someone near death."



129

00:10:48.458 --> 00:10:50.833

You guys...



130

00:10:50.833 --> 00:10:53.917

Do you have the faintest damn clue...



131

00:10:53.917 --> 00:10:55.917

...what you're doing?



132

00:10:57.250 --> 00:10:59.458

It's Erwin...



133

00:10:59.458 --> 00:11:02.500

The commander of the Scouts.



134

00:11:02.500 --> 00:11:05.250

And you're saying to watch him die.



135

00:11:06.708 --> 00:11:08.583

There's no time for this.



136

00:11:08.583 --> 00:11:10.500

Stay out of my way.



137

00:11:13.208 --> 00:11:16.667

Keep your emotions out of this.



138

00:11:16.667 --> 00:11:20.542

Keep my... emotions out?



139

00:11:20.542 --> 00:11:25.250

Tell me... How come you didn't

hand over the syringe right away?!



140

00:11:25.250 --> 00:11:30.333

Because I was considering the

possibility Erwin might still be alive.



141

00:11:30.333 --> 00:11:34.167

You couldn't have known Floch

would drag the commander here!



142

00:11:34.167 --> 00:11:36.833

There's just no way you knew!



143

00:11:36.833 --> 00:11:38.667

You're right, but...



144

00:11:38.667 --> 00:11:42.875

The fact that Erwin is now here

means I use it on him.



145

00:11:54.958 --> 00:11:56.292

Hey!



146

00:11:58.292 --> 00:12:00.667

His strength isn't all there!



147

00:12:00.667 --> 00:12:03.125

I can take it from him by force!



148

00:12:03.125 --> 00:12:05.500

You should know as well as I do!



149

00:12:05.500 --> 00:12:09.625

Without Erwin's talent,

humanity can't beat the Titans!



150

00:12:09.625 --> 00:12:14.000

That's right, Mikasa! Let's stop

with this madness already!



151

00:12:16.500 --> 00:12:21.792

It's... no different if we lose... Armin.



152

00:12:21.792 --> 00:12:23.458

Eren!



153

00:12:23.458 --> 00:12:27.125

Hasn't it... always been like that?



154

00:12:27.125 --> 00:12:31.333

He's the reason why we saved

Trost by plugging it with a rock.



155

00:12:31.333 --> 00:12:34.292

He revealed Annie's identity.



156

00:12:34.292 --> 00:12:38.417

It was Armin who came up with

the idea of moving at night!



157

00:12:38.417 --> 00:12:41.667

The only reason we uncovered

Reiner's hiding spot...



158

00:12:41.667 --> 00:12:44.333

...and the only reason we defeated Bertholdt...



159

00:12:44.333 --> 00:12:48.167

...was all because of Armin!



160

00:12:48.167 --> 00:12:52.375

The one who's gonna save humanity

isn't me or the commander!



161

00:12:52.375 --> 00:12:54.042

It's Armin!



162

00:12:54.042 --> 00:12:56.125

Isn't that right, Mikasa?!



163

00:12:59.167 --> 00:13:01.708

Please give it to me!



164

00:13:05.667 --> 00:13:09.042

The one who will save humanity...

is Commander Erwin.



165

00:13:09.042 --> 00:13:11.042

Shut up!



166

00:13:11.042 --> 00:13:12.958

I will not shut up.



167

00:13:12.958 --> 00:13:16.083

Don't think you're the only

ones who've had it tough!



168

00:13:16.083 --> 00:13:18.042

You might not know, but...



169

00:13:18.042 --> 00:13:22.583

On the other side of that wall,

there's not a single living soldier.



170

00:13:22.583 --> 00:13:26.458

Everyone died when the Beast

Titan threw boulders at us.



171

00:13:26.458 --> 00:13:29.792

I didn't think anyone could be saved...



172

00:13:29.792 --> 00:13:33.750

But Commander Erwin was the only exception.



173

00:13:33.750 --> 00:13:38.750

He thought of a plan for us

to bite back at the Beast Titan...



174

00:13:38.750 --> 00:13:41.042

...and we did.



175

00:13:41.042 --> 00:13:44.208

We were smashed to bits just as planned.



176

00:13:46.542 --> 00:13:50.375

And I'm sure the last thing they felt...



177

00:13:50.375 --> 00:13:52.333

...was fear.



178

00:13:58.958 --> 00:14:04.458

When I found the commander alive,

I was about to finish him off.



179

00:14:06.208 --> 00:14:11.333

But... that's going too easy on him.



180

00:14:11.333 --> 00:14:15.750

I thought to myself that he ought

to taste more of this hell.



181

00:14:17.917 --> 00:14:21.208

And then... I understood.



182

00:14:23.458 --> 00:14:28.250

The only one who can lay waste

to the Titans... is a devil!



183

00:14:28.250 --> 00:14:33.542

And if I can bring back the devil,

that must be my mission in life!



184

00:14:33.542 --> 00:14:38.917

That has to be why I survived like

a coward when everyone else died!



185

00:14:38.917 --> 00:14:40.708

So stay out of his way!



186

00:14:40.708 --> 00:14:41.833

Don't do it!



187

00:14:45.875 --> 00:14:47.292

Hange...



188

00:14:51.333 --> 00:14:56.042

Hey... You've got to be... kidding me...



189

00:14:56.042 --> 00:14:57.708

No way...



190

00:15:00.292 --> 00:15:03.458

You can't... be serious...



191

00:15:10.833 --> 00:15:15.667

Mikasa! You have to know

how much we need Erwin!



192

00:15:15.667 --> 00:15:20.042

We can't let the flames of hope

extinguish inside the walls!



193

00:15:20.042 --> 00:15:23.667

But... Armin could... do that, too!



194

00:15:23.667 --> 00:15:26.583

It's true, Armin is exceptional...



195

00:15:26.583 --> 00:15:30.667

But he doesn't have Erwin's

experience and leadership!



196

00:15:35.958 --> 00:15:40.208

There are people I want to bring back, too.



197

00:15:40.208 --> 00:15:42.125

Hundreds of them.



198

00:15:45.458 --> 00:15:50.000

I've had to say farewell since

the day I joined the Scouts.



199

00:15:50.000 --> 00:15:51.375

Hange!



200

00:16:07.083 --> 00:16:08.875

But...



201

00:16:08.875 --> 00:16:11.167

You know, don't you?



202

00:16:11.167 --> 00:16:15.542

No matter who it is,

there comes a day to say farewell.



203

00:16:19.000 --> 00:16:23.708

I know it's impossible,

but you have to accept this.



204

00:16:23.708 --> 00:16:27.583

There will be times you can't keep your sanity.



205

00:16:27.583 --> 00:16:29.292

It's tough.



206

00:16:29.292 --> 00:16:30.875

Very tough.



207

00:16:30.875 --> 00:16:33.042

I know.



208

00:16:33.042 --> 00:16:37.208

Even so, we have to keep moving forward.



209

00:17:00.042 --> 00:17:01.792

Captain...



210

00:17:02.917 --> 00:17:08.042

Do you... know about... the sea?



211

00:17:08.042 --> 00:17:13.000

No matter how far you look,

it stretches past the horizon.



212

00:17:13.000 --> 00:17:15.750

It's a gigantic lake.



213

00:17:16.792 --> 00:17:17.750

Armin said--



214

00:17:17.750 --> 00:17:20.667

Hey! Cut it out!



215

00:17:20.667 --> 00:17:23.958

There's a sea beyond the walls...



216

00:17:23.958 --> 00:17:27.417

...and he said we'd go there together!



217

00:17:27.417 --> 00:17:33.708

But... that was our dream since we

were little, and I forgot it long ago!



218

00:17:33.708 --> 00:17:38.042

Avenging my mom... Killing the Titans...



219

00:17:38.042 --> 00:17:41.417

The only thoughts in my head are full of hate!



220

00:17:41.417 --> 00:17:45.208

But... he's not like that!



221

00:17:45.208 --> 00:17:48.125

Armin cares about more than just fighting!



222

00:17:48.125 --> 00:17:50.417

He has dreams!



223

00:17:54.042 --> 00:17:56.417

Everyone get out of here!



224

00:17:56.417 --> 00:18:00.417

I'm going to have Erwin eat Bertholdt!



225

00:18:01.875 --> 00:18:04.250

Come on. Let's go, Mikasa.



226

00:18:04.250 --> 00:18:06.708

Shit... Shit...!



227

00:18:09.292 --> 00:18:11.583

Armin...



228

00:18:11.583 --> 00:18:13.083

See you...



229

00:18:24.708 --> 00:18:28.125

Let's start by seeing the sea!



230

00:18:28.125 --> 00:18:31.333

You'll see! It does exist!



231

00:18:35.542 --> 00:18:37.750

If this dream of yours comes true...



232

00:18:37.750 --> 00:18:39.917

...what will you do then?



233

00:18:39.917 --> 00:18:44.625

I don't know. I won't know until it happens.



234

00:18:44.625 --> 00:18:46.792

I...



235

00:18:46.792 --> 00:18:49.250

I want to go to the basement.



236

00:18:50.417 --> 00:18:52.292

Good grief.



237

00:18:52.292 --> 00:18:55.417

They're all the same...



238

00:18:55.417 --> 00:18:58.500

Whining like brats one after another...



239

00:18:58.500 --> 00:19:05.333

Everyone had to be drunk on

somethin' to keep pushing on...



240

00:19:05.333 --> 00:19:10.250

Everyone... was a slave to somethin'.



241

00:19:10.250 --> 00:19:12.667

But there's more than that.



242

00:19:12.667 --> 00:19:14.250

The sea...



243

00:19:21.625 --> 00:19:23.208

Erwin!



244

00:19:24.208 --> 00:19:26.458

Teacher...



245

00:19:26.458 --> 00:19:30.875

How do we know there're not more humans...



246

00:19:30.875 --> 00:19:34.292

...outside the walls?



247

00:19:42.583 --> 00:19:45.292

Give up on your dream and die.



248

00:19:45.292 --> 00:19:48.375

Lead the recruits straight into hell.



249

00:19:48.375 --> 00:19:53.792

Everyone had to be drunk on

somethin' to keep pushing on...



250

00:19:53.792 --> 00:19:57.292

I will take down the Beast Titan.



251

00:20:07.458 --> 00:20:09.292

Levi...



252

00:20:09.292 --> 00:20:11.000

Thank you.



253

00:20:44.958 --> 00:20:46.542

Guys!



254

00:20:46.542 --> 00:20:49.375

Help me!



255

00:20:54.792 --> 00:20:59.167

Annie! Reiner!



256

00:21:02.417 --> 00:21:04.208

Captain...



257

00:21:04.208 --> 00:21:06.792

Why... did you...?



258

00:21:09.583 --> 00:21:14.333

Do you think... you can forgive him?



259

00:21:14.333 --> 00:21:17.375

He had no choice but to become a devil.



260

00:21:18.583 --> 00:21:21.333

It was us who wished for that.



261

00:21:22.292 --> 00:21:27.375

And in the end, when he had

finally been set free from hell,



262

00:21:27.375 --> 00:21:31.250

we wanted to bring him back once more.



263

00:21:31.250 --> 00:21:35.667

But I think... it's time to let him rest.



264

00:21:47.375 --> 00:21:49.125

Erwin...



265

00:21:49.125 --> 00:21:51.958

I promised I'd kill the Beast Titan, but...



266

00:21:51.958 --> 00:21:55.083

It's going to have to wait.



267

00:21:55.083 --> 00:21:58.000

He's... dead.



268

00:22:01.917 --> 00:22:03.708

I see.



269

00:23:58.250 --> 00:24:03.042

Armin is shaken after learning

of Bertholdt's and Erwin's deaths.



270

00:24:03.042 --> 00:24:09.250

Eren heads towards that place his father,

Grisha, promised to show him.



271

00:24:09.250 --> 00:24:12.096

Next episode: "The Basement."

